1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,013
[Birthday Preparation]
(note: the prologue is voiceless, but the date+birthday event is still voiced!)

2
00:00:02,013 --> 00:00:05,721
Little Kid A: [Little Kid A] MC-jiejie, please have some cookies, they’re really yummy!

3
00:00:05,721 --> 00:00:08,566
Little Kid B: [Little Kid B] Don’t listen to him, MC-jiejie… Here, have some filled chocolates. They’re a thousand times yummier than his~

4
00:00:08,566 --> 00:00:10,196
Little Kid C: [Little Kid C] I’ve got something tasty too. Here, it’s for you.

5
00:00:10,196 --> 00:00:13,648
In the orphanage, the children crowd around me with such enthusiasm that I end up sitting helplessly on the lawn, accepting a cookie from one side and a chocolate from the other.

6
00:00:13,648 --> 00:00:15,821
MC: Thank you, everyone! I’ll make sure to eat every last one…

7
00:00:15,821 --> 00:00:19,241
Before I even finish speaking, a ringtone abruptly rings out. I pick up my phone to see Lucien’s call invitation strikingly pop up on the screen.

8
00:00:19,241 --> 00:00:22,981
The little girl leaning on my shoulder keenly recognizes the profile picture on the screen and claps her hands in excitement, exclaiming—

9
00:00:22,981 --> 00:00:24,451
Little Girl: [Little Girl] It’s Lucien-gege!

10
00:00:24,451 --> 00:00:26,433
Children: [Children] Lucien-gege?! Is he coming to play with us too?

11
00:00:26,433 --> 00:00:29,309
Looking at the children around me, their heads tilted up and their eyes sparkling with stars, I can’t help but laugh as I rise to my feet, gently placing my index finger to my lips.

12
00:00:29,309 --> 00:00:31,803
MC: Shh… I’m going to answer Lucien-gege’s call now. Don’t follow me for now, okay?

13
00:00:31,803 --> 00:00:34,487
MC: Otherwise, if he sees us all gathered together, he’ll immediately guess that we’re preparing a birthday surprise for him.

14
00:00:34,487 --> 00:00:36,693
Children: [Children] Right, right, right. Lucien-gege is the smartest, we can’t let him find out!

15
00:00:36,693 --> 00:00:39,282
The children all cover their mouths with their small hands and watch me walk to a tree in the distance.

16
00:00:39,282 --> 00:00:41,615
When I pick up my phone again, I discover that the call invitation from just now has already expired.

17
00:00:41,615 --> 00:00:44,556
A little fox sticker has appeared in the chatbox. It’s lying on the ground, wagging its tail, with a speech bubble popping up next to its head —

18
00:00:44,556 --> 00:00:46,026
“Are you busy?”

19
00:00:46,026 --> 00:00:49,734
I let out a soft puff of laughter and hurriedly called him back.

20
00:00:49,734 --> 00:00:52,163
MC: I really was busy a moment ago, but I’m free now.

21
00:00:52,163 --> 00:00:54,209
Lucien: What were you busy with? Is there anything I can help with?

22
00:00:54,209 --> 00:00:56,126
MC: Hmm… no! Everything’s going smoothly right now~

23
00:00:56,126 --> 00:00:58,971
Perhaps my momentary hesitation exposes something; he immediately lets out an involuntary laugh, his clear voice sounding once more.

24
00:00:58,971 --> 00:01:00,473
Lucien: Okay, I understand.

25
00:01:00,473 --> 00:01:02,743
Lucien: As the soon-to-be birthday boy, I will quietly await all of Miss Producer’s arrangements.

26
00:01:02,743 --> 00:01:04,021
MC: ….!

27
00:01:04,021 --> 00:01:06,003
MC: Wait, I didn’t say I was busy with your birthday.

28
00:01:06,003 --> 00:01:07,793
Lucien: Mm, MC didn’t say that.

29
00:01:07,793 --> 00:01:10,510
Lucien: But your tone of voice, your laughter, and your busy figure these past few days have always been quietly telling me—

30
00:01:10,510 --> 00:01:12,651
Lucien: Late autumn has arrived, and the joy you’ve prepared for me is also close at hand.

31
00:01:12,651 --> 00:01:14,697
My heart softens, and my voice unconsciously follows his, gentling considerably.

32
00:01:14,697 --> 00:01:17,254
MC: As expected, it’s hard to keep anything from you, but you’ll never guess what surprise I’ve prepared for you this year~

33
00:01:17,254 --> 00:01:19,683
Lucien: Of course, because our Miss Producer always has the ability to take people by surprise.

34
00:01:19,683 --> 00:01:21,984
Lucien: So it’s not just this year. In fact, I’ve found it difficult to guess in every past year.

35
00:01:21,984 --> 00:01:24,797
Lucien: Even though many of the details have long been readily apparent, I still feel surprised and happy about everything you do.

36
00:01:24,797 --> 00:01:27,674
MC: Then please continue to look forward to it, Professor Xu.

37
00:01:27,674 --> 00:01:30,646
As I say this, I turn around. Seeing the children sitting on the lawn with their gazes still fixed on me, I smile and give them a small wave.

38
00:01:30,646 --> 00:01:32,788
MC: This year… I will continue to make you feel happiness too.

39
00:01:41,066 --> 00:01:45,221
Dawn is just breaking. The still-lit street lamps stretch out halos of light, and the world seems steeped in a hazy gray-blue.

40
00:01:45,221 --> 00:01:50,463
A rich rice aroma seeps through the gap in the pot lid. Amidst the steady bubbling sounds, a faint chime of the elevator arriving comes from the hallway. I quickly turn off the stove and hurry toward the entryway.

41
00:01:50,463 --> 00:01:54,395
Sure enough, before long, the front door is gently pushed open.

42
00:01:54,395 --> 00:01:58,933
As our eyes meet, Lucien seems to freeze for a moment. Then his brows and eyes curve in understanding, and he watches as I step forward and wrap him in an embrace.

43
00:01:58,933 --> 00:02:01,395
MC: Good morning, Professor Xu.

44
00:02:01,395 --> 00:02:06,892
The arms encircling me naturally tighten, and with immense tenderness, he envelops me in his windbreaker, keeping the chill clinging to him from settling onto me too much.

45
00:02:06,892 --> 00:02:10,824
After a moment’s delay, his low voice comes through.

46
00:02:10,824 --> 00:02:13,796
Lucien: Good morning, MC.

47
00:02:13,796 --> 00:02:21,403
Lucien: If I had known you would be waiting for me here, I should have “warmed myself up” a bit first.

48
00:02:21,403 --> 00:02:24,887
MC: That won’t do, I always want to see you a little earlier.

49
00:02:24,887 --> 00:02:27,157
I lift my head from his embrace.

50
00:02:27,157 --> 00:02:30,992
MC: And while waiting for you, I’ve already prepared a loving breakfast for Mr. Birthday Star~

51
00:02:30,992 --> 00:02:35,851
MC: On a special day like this, waking up a little earlier, preparing and waiting seems to make the whole day feel longer than usual.

52
00:02:35,851 --> 00:02:38,727
Lucien: Did you wake up very early?

53
00:02:38,727 --> 00:02:43,713
MC: Probably not long after you left. Don’t worry, you didn’t wake me. I just wanted today to begin earlier.

54
00:02:43,713 --> 00:02:46,782
Before I knew it, I had already started to get used to the days of celebrating Lucien’s birthday in Loveland City.

55
00:02:46,782 --> 00:02:52,919
On this day, he also seems to have begun getting used to first going somewhere at dawn to meet someone important, and I have some guesses about where that might be.

56
00:02:52,919 --> 00:02:56,786
It’s just that since he doesn’t mention it, I don’t ask either.

57
00:02:56,786 --> 00:03:00,910
This day belongs to him, and I never want to force him to fulfill any of my hopes.

58
00:03:00,910 --> 00:03:05,065
Lucien doesn’t speak for a moment; his gaze falls heavily upon me like a lingering kiss.

59
00:03:05,065 --> 00:03:09,539
After a moment, he rests his chin against the top of my head and nuzzles gently.

60
00:03:09,539 --> 00:03:18,873
Lucien: I think I felt it too. I felt it from the very moment I saw you just now.

61
00:03:18,873 --> 00:03:28,174
Lucien: Today indeed has been a long one. Yet even now, I still want time to slow down just a little more.

62
00:03:28,174 --> 00:03:33,767
MC: I’ll go along with whatever you want, Mr. Birthday Star~

63
00:03:33,767 --> 00:03:39,201
After I say that, I pull him to sit at the dining table, bring out the breakfast made with love that I’ve been keeping warm in the pot one dish at a time, and even arrange the plates with a touch of ceremony.

64
00:03:39,201 --> 00:03:43,644
The soft, glutinous longevity peach buns emanate aromas of custard and red bean paste, sitting upright atop the slightly crooked carrot-carved characters spelling ‘Happy Birthday’.

65
00:03:43,644 --> 00:03:50,196
Lucien: Can I eat all of these too?

66
00:03:50,196 --> 00:03:54,767
Seeing his gaze linger on those few ‘masterpieces’ I made on a whim, I quickly pick up a longevity peach bun and set it into his bowl.

67
00:03:54,767 --> 00:03:57,995
MC: Those are just for decoration.

68
00:03:57,995 --> 00:04:02,342
Lucien: But they also blessings meant for me.

69
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:06,913
He says it with such earnestness as though it were the most natural thing in the world. Left completely unable to do anything about him, I can only surrender.

70
00:04:06,913 --> 00:04:10,844
MC: Okay, I’ve already said that I’ll go along with whatever you want!

71
00:04:10,844 --> 00:04:13,242
Smiling, I open my arms toward him.

72
00:04:13,242 --> 00:04:14,712
MC: Happy birthday—

73
00:04:14,712 --> 00:04:17,684
MC: Let’s start a day of surprises that belongs only to Lucien—

74
00:04:17,684 --> 00:04:22,191
The steam from the breakfast haze in front of him, making it seem as if he is slowly returning from a very distant place to my side, and he gently lifts a smile.

75
00:04:22,191 --> 00:04:27,785
Lucien: I’m looking forward to it.

76
00:04:33,410 --> 00:04:37,406
When the car stops at the orphanage’s main gate, a few children who can hardly contain themselves come scrambling out and surround Lucien.

77
00:04:37,406 --> 00:04:40,442
Boy A: We’ve been waiting for you for so long, big birthday star! Waaah…

78
00:04:40,442 --> 00:04:44,214
Girl A: You’re so silly! That’s part of the later segment, don’t ruin the surprise!

79
00:04:44,214 --> 00:04:47,602
Girl A: Come on, gege and jiejie, everyone is inside~

80
00:04:47,602 --> 00:04:51,022
Without waiting for a reply, the girl grabs our hands and tugs us forward.

81
00:04:51,022 --> 00:04:55,145
Childish cheers crash over us without warning like waves, and Lucien seems unusually a bit slow to respond.

82
00:04:55,145 --> 00:05:00,579
He subconsciously bends forward a little, letting the children crowd around him, and amid their noisy chatter and cheerful laughter, he plays along with this “highest-level” welcoming ceremony.

83
00:05:00,579 --> 00:05:05,565
I seldom see Lucien with such an uncharacteristically overwhelmed look, and I can’t help but laugh, prompting him to turn back and look at me.

84
00:05:05,565 --> 00:05:10,551
But I simply smile, then join in the liveliness, crowding together with them.

85
00:05:10,551 --> 00:05:16,464
Lucien: ……

86
00:05:16,464 --> 00:05:19,916
MC: Let’s walk a bit faster~

87
00:05:19,916 --> 00:05:21,706
Children: Yay—!

88
00:05:21,706 --> 00:05:25,062
Like Lucien, they are all children of the world.

89
00:05:25,062 --> 00:05:30,048
And I, just like them, only want to hold up every blessing and all that is wonderful, and offer it before him.

90
00:05:31,263 --> 00:05:36,537
After leading us to the decorated small garden, the children then mysteriously left under the orphanage director’s guidance.

91
00:05:36,537 --> 00:05:43,153
The afternoon sunlight is soft, spilling at a slant into the small garden of this courtyard.

92
00:05:43,153 --> 00:05:49,738
Lucien’s gaze moves from the meticulously arranged tables and chairs to the colorful balloon decorations, then lands on the piled-up gift boxes.

93
00:05:49,738 --> 00:05:54,372
I follow his sight, see the corners of his lips lift lightly, and I smile as well.

94
00:05:54,372 --> 00:05:57,728
MC: It’s rare to see our Great Professor Xu looking this surprised.

95
00:05:57,728 --> 00:06:05,623
Lucien: I also thought that I’d already grown accustomed to accepting the miracles you bring me.

96
00:06:05,623 --> 00:06:10,194
Lucien: But indeed, you always find a way.

97
00:06:10,194 --> 00:06:14,956
MC: Hehe, then I will assuredly take that as a compliment meaning ‘you like it a lot’~

98
00:06:14,956 --> 00:06:21,509
Lucien: How could I possibly not like it?

99
00:06:21,509 --> 00:06:27,230
As the breeze brushes past, the light strands entwined among the branches and leaves sway. Dappled light refracts into Lucien’s eyes, making me unable to stop myself from indulgently sinking into them.

100
00:06:27,230 --> 00:06:31,098
MC: Even though it’s a surprise, it was still something I took the liberty of deciding on my own.

101
00:06:31,098 --> 00:06:35,476
MC: When I came to visit the children before, they invited me to watch the play they were rehearsing for today, but I accidentally let it slip.

102
00:06:35,476 --> 00:06:39,120
MC: Later they insisted on celebrating together for you. I feel that everyone’s goodwill should not be let down, and besides…

103
00:06:39,120 --> 00:06:43,467
MC: I also wanted to make your birthday a little livelier.

104
00:06:43,467 --> 00:06:46,823
I reach out and hook my finger with his.

105
00:06:46,823 --> 00:06:49,316
MC: Would this bother you?

106
00:06:49,316 --> 00:06:54,494
Lucien doesn’t speak for a moment, his fingertips’ pads stroking my knuckles. Then he takes my hand and guides it to rest against his chest.

107
00:06:54,494 --> 00:07:01,942
Lucien: MC, I smell the fragrance of flowers, the scent of fresh grass, and even the aroma of clouds…

108
00:07:01,942 --> 00:07:15,846
Lucien: I hear the children’s voices, and your voice. These sounds of laughter, these heartbeats… are unexpectedly rich.

109
00:07:15,846 --> 00:07:21,311
Lucien: It makes me momentarily not know what to do.

110
00:07:21,311 --> 00:07:28,279
Lucien: Would this count as a bother?

111
00:07:28,279 --> 00:07:31,987
This does not seem to be a question, nor exactly an answer.

112
00:07:31,987 --> 00:07:35,758
But looking into those eyes brimming with a smile, all I want to do is kiss him.

113
00:07:35,758 --> 00:07:39,115
So I rise onto my toes, tilt my face up, and lean in.

114
00:07:39,115 --> 00:07:42,439
??: MC-jiejie! Lucien-gege! Ah….

115
00:07:42,439 --> 00:07:49,311
I instinctively stop and, turning my head, see the boy who had been running at the front come to a halt with an innocent look on his face. In one motion, he tosses the prop planet in his hand away and covers his eyes.

116
00:07:49,311 --> 00:07:52,123
MC: Pffft…

117
00:07:52,571 --> 00:07:59,027
Before I can speak, Lucien already turns me towards him, lifts his hand to cradle my face, and a series of delicate kisses rains down.

118
00:07:59,027 --> 00:08:07,881
Lucien: As you said, we simply can’t disappoint the children’s ‘goodwill’.

119
00:08:07,881 --> 00:08:12,931
His murmured voice brushes close to my lips, lingering with tender reluctance to part.

120
00:08:14,082 --> 00:08:19,196
Soon, the children return to this world’s ‘stage’, dressed in their performance outfits and carrying a variety of handmade props.

121
00:08:19,196 --> 00:08:25,525
As they flock around Lucien with their rhythmic, tiny footsteps, I move to the outer perimeter as rehearsed and press play on the music.

122
00:08:25,525 --> 00:08:32,429
After everyone decided to prepare a surprise celebration for Lucien, they then adapted the Little Prince play they had originally planned to perform into a story of the Little Prince celebrating his birthday.

123
00:08:32,429 --> 00:08:35,465
And naturally, I also took part in preparing this surprise.

124
00:08:35,465 --> 00:08:40,356
Today is the Little Prince’s birthday, and the whole planet comes to offer him their blessings.

125
00:08:40,356 --> 00:08:44,862
The boy wearing the fox-eared headband takes two steps forward and makes a gentlemanly gesture of welcome toward Lucien.

126
00:08:44,862 --> 00:08:47,803
Boy: [Boy] Happy birthday, our Little Prince.

127
00:08:47,803 --> 00:08:53,364
Boy: [Boy] Today is the day the stars sent you into this world. On such a special day, all of us are here to celebrate your birthday with you.

128
00:08:53,364 --> 00:08:59,949
Girl: [Girl] This is the crown we wove for you with the blessings of the entire planet. Our planet may be small, but here, you will never, ever be alone.

129
00:08:59,949 --> 00:09:06,469
The “little sheep” with cotton hair ties takes out a woven flower wreath from behind, the colorful blossoms interwoven and nestled together like a gathered piece of heavy autumn radiance.

130
00:09:06,469 --> 00:09:11,839
Lucien cooperates by sitting down on the grass and slightly bowing his head, allowing the wreath to be reverently placed upon his head like a crown.

131
00:09:13,086 --> 00:09:17,209
Girl: [Girl] Little Prince, welcome to this planet.

132
00:09:17,209 --> 00:09:23,314
Boy: [Boy] We like you, and we want to be your best friends for a lifetime.

133
00:09:23,314 --> 00:09:29,387
The children of the earth celebrate the arrival of their friend, forgetting their sorrow and sadness, sincere yet also clumsy.

134
00:09:29,387 --> 00:09:34,181
They join me in wishing him happiness.

135
00:09:34,181 --> 00:09:38,720
What is a birthday?

136
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:43,834
It is the day the Earth revolves back to where it first saw the sun, the day the stars draw a little closer, the day the wind is gentle and the sunlight warm.

137
00:09:43,834 --> 00:09:49,555
And now, it is also a day when he is no longer alone, no longer needs to watch forty-four sunsets by himself.

138
00:09:49,555 --> 00:09:55,468
Naive children may not deeply comprehend what’s being conveyed, yet perhaps they sense it more keenly and understand it more clearly than anyone else.

139
00:09:55,468 --> 00:10:00,199
Bang-pop!

140
00:10:00,199 --> 00:10:06,591
In an instant, the colorful paper pieces and flower confetti burst into the air, drifting and swaying as they fall onto every smiling face, like a dazzling fireworks display.

141
00:10:06,591 --> 00:10:10,683
At the same time, I hand Lucien a little cake.

142
00:10:10,683 --> 00:10:16,276
It’s plain and small, but the childlike piping is really moving, and the drawn candle looks like wishes that will never fall.

143
00:10:16,276 --> 00:10:21,582
The child who set off the confetti lifts both of his hands high with a hearty laugh, as if only in this way can he firmly hold the overflowing blessings.

144
00:10:21,582 --> 00:10:25,290
Lucien holds the cake in one hand and gently rubs the head of the child in front of him with the other.

145
00:10:25,290 --> 00:10:29,828
Lucien: Thank you everyone.

146
00:10:29,828 --> 00:10:34,879
Lucien: Thank you everyone, for coming to celebrate my birthday.

147
00:10:34,879 --> 00:10:40,280
Children & MC: Happy birthday to you, happy birthday to you…

148
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:43,828
MC: Happy birthday!!

149
00:10:43,828 --> 00:10:49,741
Children: Make a wish, make a wish! Gege‘s wish will definitely come true—

150
00:10:49,741 --> 00:10:53,385
The shimmering, radiant light melts into his lowered eyes.

151
00:10:54,632 --> 00:11:00,832
Lucien gazes at the childlike yet warm flame, and like a child, he obligingly closes his eyes.

152
00:11:06,714 --> 00:11:12,339
When leaving the orphanage, Lucien thanks the children one by one with heartfelt care and promises to see them again.

153
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:16,974
As if in a trance, I feel no difference in age or identity in this moment—just similar tender hearts touching each other.

154
00:11:16,974 --> 00:11:20,841
Since it’s still early, we decide on a whim to find a place to stop the car and take a stroll around.

155
00:11:20,841 --> 00:11:25,508
The flowing daylight soaks everything until it softens. Somehow, I suddenly think of some distant memories and give Lucien’s palm a little squeeze.

156
00:11:25,508 --> 00:11:29,343
MC: More and more people know your real birthday now.

157
00:11:29,343 --> 00:11:33,786
Realizing what I’m talking about, he blinks his eyes.

158
00:11:33,786 --> 00:11:40,466
Lucien: It seems I’ve… never imagined a day like this.

159
00:11:40,466 --> 00:11:46,635
He says it sincerely, his tone full of thought, which makes me unable to hold back a smile, and I can’t help but look toward him.

160
00:11:47,179 --> 00:11:54,882
The halo of light veils the ends of his hair in gold, making it look soft and fluffy, so close I can reach it.

161
00:11:56,288 --> 00:12:01,402
As we enter a small park, transparent bubbles occasionally drift past us. Iridescent, weightless, yet also ephemeral.

162
00:12:01,402 --> 00:12:06,804
We tacitly slow our pace, sinking into this romantic tranquility.

163
00:12:06,804 --> 00:12:11,534
The sparse, scattered shadows of the trees along the path fall upon him, dappling his form in alternating light and shadow.

164
00:12:11,534 --> 00:12:19,142
To this day, looking back time and again, those small things he once kept hidden have come to feel like a unique kind of demarcation and welcoming invitation.

165
00:12:19,142 --> 00:12:25,438
Such uniqueness is captivating, but I’m always afraid that he will be alone.

166
00:12:25,438 --> 00:12:30,680
Lucien notices my gaze and my silence; he doesn’t speak and simply looks toward me.

167
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:35,475
I gently shake our clasped palms.

168
00:12:35,475 --> 00:12:37,840
MC: Lucien, I’m really so greedy.

169
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:45,447
MC: Sometimes I wish that everything about you belonged only to me, that all your secrets, joys, and sorrows were known to me alone.

170
00:12:45,447 --> 00:12:50,529
MC: But sometimes I want to surround you with even more warmth, and let you enjoy all the praise and blessings from the whole world.

171
00:12:50,529 --> 00:12:55,995
Lucien: It seems MC has become just like me too.

172
00:12:55,995 --> 00:13:00,342
MC: Besides the genius-level mind and knowledge, I’ve long since become like Professor Xu.

173
00:13:00,342 --> 00:13:07,629
Lucien: Then be even greedier, I want you to be greedy for me.

174
00:13:07,629 --> 00:13:10,826
MC: Really? Then there will be two greedy ones in our home!

175
00:13:10,826 --> 00:13:19,328
Lucien: It sounds like something that would bring joy.

176
00:13:19,328 --> 00:13:24,889
He crinkles his eyes, speaking so naturally and earnestly that I can’t help but laugh too.

177
00:13:24,889 --> 00:13:29,172
Suddenly, Lucien notices something I can’t see; his line of sight lingers behind me for a moment. Before I can curiously turn to look, he pulls me into a run.

178
00:13:29,172 --> 00:13:34,670
Lucien: MC, I want to play that.

179
00:13:34,670 --> 00:13:37,323
MC: Huh?

180
00:13:37,323 --> 00:13:40,903
Hearing such straightforward words come from his mouth, I momentarily think I must have misheard.

181
00:13:40,903 --> 00:13:47,519
Hearing such straightforward words come from his mouth, I momentarily think I must have misheard.

182
00:13:47,519 --> 00:13:54,295
The small circular platform lies quietly within a transparent, circular ‘bubble dome’, swaying in the sunlight and giving off a kaleidoscope of colors.

183
00:13:54,295 --> 00:13:59,985
The children in front of us run ahead in high spirits; one steps up onto the platform, while the other squats down outside it, gripping the golden pull-rod connected to the pump.

184
00:13:59,985 --> 00:14:05,482
The children in front of us run ahead in high spirits; one steps up onto the platform, while the other squats down outside it, gripping the golden pull-rod connected to the pump.

185
00:14:05,482 --> 00:14:11,012
The children in front of us run ahead in high spirits; one steps up onto the platform, while the other squats down outside it, gripping the golden pull-rod connected to the pump.

186
00:14:11,491 --> 00:14:14,943
Lucien: It’s our turn.

187
00:14:14,943 --> 00:14:20,760
Lucien pulls me to the center of the round platform.

188
00:14:20,760 --> 00:14:25,491
MC: Are we both supposed to stand inside? But this seems like it needs someone to be outside…

189
00:14:25,491 --> 00:14:29,199
Before I can finish speaking, he pulls me into his arms in one swift motion, gazing at me with eyes brimming with a smile.

190
00:14:29,199 --> 00:14:35,208
With a barely perceptible sound, the pull-rod at our feet seems to be pulled by an invisible force, slowly rising—

191
00:14:36,422 --> 00:14:43,582
The soft film gradually rises, drawing the flowing world around it into itself and spreading a rainbow-hued halo.

192
00:14:43,582 --> 00:14:48,792
Like huge transparent petals, blooming and closing, both hazy and dreamlike.

193
00:14:48,792 --> 00:14:53,874
It gently yet firmly envelops us, immersing us in the midst of its dazzling yet fragile life.

194
00:14:53,874 --> 00:14:59,947
As if it were a transparent universe.

195
00:14:59,947 --> 00:15:05,828
Lucien places my palm against his chest, the strong, solid pulsation seeming to seep along my fingertips toward my heart.

196
00:15:05,828 --> 00:15:16,472
Lucien: Birth, brilliance, struggle… then silently dissolves into foam.

197
00:15:16,472 --> 00:15:22,609
Lucien: For me, the world is often like this.

198
00:15:22,609 --> 00:15:30,951
Lucien: I can see it clearly, yet I don’t necessarily need to approach and feel it.

199
00:15:30,951 --> 00:15:46,549
Lucien: But then, you are here. I feel your warmth and scent, as if they were the warmth and scent of the world itself.

200
00:15:46,549 --> 00:15:58,631
Lucien: It can feel cramped, confining, even make me want to leave or push it away, and yet…

201
00:15:58,631 --> 00:16:11,224
Lucien: And yet, I still feel a kind of indefinable happiness, one I can neither let go of, nor bear to part with.

202
00:16:11,224 --> 00:16:15,156
His voice is soft, yet it lands heavily upon my heart.

203
00:16:15,156 --> 00:16:21,452
It’s as if something is continually clamoring into bloom within my chest, leaving me at a loss for words. All I can do is look back at him.

204
00:16:21,452 --> 00:16:32,064
Lucien: Even if it hangs suspended in the air, I still want to touch its existence and witness its dazzling radiance.

205
00:16:32,064 --> 00:16:41,621
Sunlight streams through the bubble, refracting into a shifting, fluid iridescence.

206
00:16:43,027 --> 00:16:48,109
As his words come to an end, the bubble bursts with a sudden pop, its colorful, glistening fragments falling all over us.

207
00:16:48,109 --> 00:16:52,456
A faint coolness slips gently into my breath, like a sweet and fleeting kiss.

208
00:16:52,456 --> 00:16:56,995
It’s the scent of bubble water, yet it also feels like the scent of contentment.

209
00:16:56,995 --> 00:17:07,063
Lucien: Then I heard a sound I’d never heard before, the sound of heartbeats.

210
00:17:07,063 --> 00:17:13,104
Lucien smiles; he looks gentle and cherishing, surrendering and happy.

211
00:17:13,104 --> 00:17:18,634
Amidst the hazy vibrancy, I watch him solemnly hand me a small rectangular paper bag.

212
00:17:18,634 --> 00:17:28,479
Lucien: MC, I want to welcome you into my life.

213
00:17:32,730 --> 00:17:36,693
After leaving this paper bag, Lucien then ‘vanishes’.

214
00:17:36,693 --> 00:17:40,944
The iridescent soap bubble dissolves into the air, as if it were a dream known to no one.

215
00:17:40,944 --> 00:17:44,844
Fortunately, hardly anyone pays attention to this little corner of ours. I act as if nothing happened, walk over to a nearby bench, and sit down, poking at the paper bag as I mutter.

216
00:17:44,844 --> 00:17:49,798
MC: Honestly, this man… he’s not allowed to misuse space-folding like this from now on— not even on his birthday!

217
00:17:49,798 --> 00:17:54,241
Actually, I don’t know what Lucien intends, but I will accompany this birthday star along whatever path he wishes to take.

218
00:17:54,241 --> 00:18:00,889
I want to understand everything he conveys and solve the riddle he has left for me.

219
00:18:00,889 --> 00:18:07,313
I carefully open the paper bag. A small train ticket lies quietly inside.

220
00:18:07,313 --> 00:18:13,450
I quickly look it up: it’s a special train that runs between downtown Loveland City and the suburbs, with only two departures a day, and the next departure time is…

221
00:18:13,450 --> 00:18:19,204
MC: There’s still two hours…

222
00:18:20,450 --> 00:18:26,843
The ample time feels like the silence and waiting Lucien has left for me. By the time I arrive at the platform, the sun has already melted into the horizon, and the sky is a soft expanse of orange-pink.

223
00:18:26,843 --> 00:18:30,678
The evening wind passes through the empty platform, letting out a long, drawn-out wail.

224
00:18:30,678 --> 00:18:33,875
Holding the ticket, I double-check the train information on the timetable, then wait anxiously.

225
00:18:33,875 --> 00:18:38,285
…until the headlights approaching from afar seize my entire field of vision.

226
00:18:38,285 --> 00:18:43,751
I see the train slowly come to a steady stop, its doors opening like a silent invitation.

227
00:18:43,751 --> 00:18:50,080
After a brief moment of daze, I step aboard without hesitation.

228
00:18:51,390 --> 00:18:57,847
Inside the carriage steeped in dusk, hanging goldfish lanterns sway with the sunset’s afterglow, their dangling tassels rocking lightly as if swimming through this stretch of warm-hued ocean.

229
00:18:57,847 --> 00:19:03,952
I instinctively turn and walk a few steps toward the carriage further back, and soon, I see that familiar figure.

230
00:19:03,952 --> 00:19:09,321
Step by step, I walk toward him, feeling my restless, clamorous heart finally settle back into its place.

231
00:19:09,321 --> 00:19:15,107
Lucien sits within the dusk, as if superimposed upon both the shadows and the blazing sunset clouds.

232
00:19:15,107 --> 00:19:19,709
I sit down across from him and look at him.

233
00:19:19,709 --> 00:19:22,842
MC: I’ve come to see you, Lucien.

234
00:19:22,842 --> 00:19:27,668
Lucien looks at me, his dark eyes surging with many complex emotions.

235
00:19:27,668 --> 00:19:38,887
Lucien: It was me who deliberately brought you here to see me. It was me… who deliberately made you board my train.

236
00:19:38,887 --> 00:19:43,841
His voice is hidden amid the rumble of the moving train, as if drifting in from someplace far away, yet it falls clearly into my ears.

237
00:19:43,841 --> 00:19:45,440
MC: I know.

238
00:19:45,440 --> 00:19:51,001
MC: But no matter what, I will come to see you. I will board this train.

239
00:19:51,001 --> 00:19:55,028
MC: I just hope… I didn’t make you wait for me too long.

240
00:19:55,476 --> 00:20:00,558
Lucien says nothing, his gaze drifting slowly toward the window. The sky, dyed with pink and purple, falls completely into his eyes.

241
00:20:00,558 --> 00:20:05,480
After a moment, he speaks softly.

242
00:20:05,480 --> 00:20:19,991
Lucien: Earlier today, I also boarded this train. From the starting station to the terminal station, I travel this journey alone.

243
00:20:19,991 --> 00:20:31,626
Lucien: Death and birth are but a fleeting moment apart; life is but a goldfish train heading into darkness.

244
00:20:31,626 --> 00:20:36,452
He says it so naturally, yet it makes my heart ache.

245
00:20:36,452 --> 00:20:53,457
Lucien: They’ve been gone for a long while, and I’ve lived alone for a long time too. But this morning, I suddenly realized… the days with you by my side have also passed for a long time without my noticing.

246
00:20:53,457 --> 00:21:01,160
Lucien: So this morning, when I was sitting here, I missed you very much.

247
00:21:01,160 --> 00:21:10,429
Lucien: Thinking of you, I felt a particular emotion.

248
00:21:10,429 --> 00:21:12,922
MC: What is it?

249
00:21:12,922 --> 00:21:18,036
Lucien: Loneliness.

250
00:21:18,036 --> 00:21:21,999
He quietly gazes at me, as if he is looking straight into the bottom of my heart.

251
00:21:21,999 --> 00:21:26,219
During the girl’s brief silence, Lucien suddenly feels a sense of peace and steadiness, the kind that comes after one’s heart has been laid bare.

252
00:21:26,219 --> 00:21:30,342
Fresh flowers, smiles, fireworks, bubbles, time, life… love.

253
00:21:30,342 --> 00:21:35,712
They are clearly so fleeting, yet why do they still stay etched in my mind?

254
00:21:35,712 --> 00:21:42,584
I know you are the answer, but why is it that you turn them into something eternal?

255
00:21:42,584 --> 00:21:49,328
In this loneliness, I replay them in my mind, and then I think of you.

256
00:21:49,328 --> 00:21:54,026
MC: And now I’m here, I’ve come to your side.

257
00:21:54,026 --> 00:22:00,930
Lucien: So I think… I will look forward to encountering them again.

258
00:22:00,930 --> 00:22:15,889
Lucien: Willingly letting them bring me dull pain, watching their blooming and their withering, allowing them to enrich my entire being.

259
00:22:15,889 --> 00:22:21,131
MC: But Lucien, you seem afraid.

260
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:25,638
Lucien: Afraid…

261
00:22:25,638 --> 00:22:31,199
He murmurs, repeating what I said, then lapses into silence.

262
00:22:31,199 --> 00:22:38,966
As the train speeds forward, I watch him pause for a long moment, then smiles reflectively.

263
00:22:38,966 --> 00:22:49,546
Lucien: So it turns out I’m also afraid.

264
00:22:49,546 --> 00:22:54,916
If life and death are separated only by a single door, if impermanence is the everyday reality of fate, if on the same day I welcome death’s arrival and birth’s celebratory song…

265
00:22:54,916 --> 00:22:59,710
Then life and death seem to hold no difference to me.

266
00:22:59,710 --> 00:23:03,418
But I’m still afraid.

267
00:23:03,418 --> 00:23:08,308
Just like when I think of those two figures, it’s as if the numbing anesthesia is wearing off, leaving me in a belated, dawning silence.

268
00:23:08,308 --> 00:23:12,751
The person before me seems somewhat at a loss and troubled, yet also incomparably vivid.

269
00:23:12,751 --> 00:23:14,924
MC: Lucien.

270
00:23:14,924 --> 00:23:18,217
I stand up and walk toward him.

271
00:23:18,217 --> 00:23:23,490
MC: You know, I actually thought for a long, long time about what gift to give you this year.

272
00:23:23,490 --> 00:23:28,668
MC: In the end, I came up with something that’s a bit special.

273
00:23:28,668 --> 00:23:35,093
As I speak, I take out from my bag a thin stack of A4 paper that I had secretly slipped in that morning. I then solemnly place it in Lucien’s hands and sit down beside him.

274
00:23:35,093 --> 00:23:40,686
He seems a little taken aback. His lowered gaze pauses briefly on the paper before returning to my face.

275
00:23:40,686 --> 00:23:45,513
Even against the backlight, I can clearly see something flickering within those beautiful eyes.

276
00:23:45,513 --> 00:23:51,554
MC: Dear Professor Xu, although it may seem a little strange as your birthday gift, what I want to give you is my, MC’s life insurance policy.

277
00:23:51,554 --> 00:23:55,709
MC: It may not have any legal effect, but I guarantee it is still valid.

278
00:23:55,709 --> 00:24:00,599
MC: Fate is capricious, and people get worn down by all kinds of partings, so I want to stay by your side, always and forever.

279
00:24:00,599 --> 00:24:05,074
MC: I don’t want you to go through dusk and dawn alone anymore. I want you to be whole from now on, and I want to be within that wholeness.

280
00:24:05,074 --> 00:24:09,165
MC: I want to turn your train into ours.

281
00:24:09,165 --> 00:24:12,202
I take his hand and draw him into my arms.

282
00:24:12,202 --> 00:24:16,197
MC: I’ve listed many possible dangers and accidents, along with compensation measures and ‘claims details’.

283
00:24:16,197 --> 00:24:21,343
MC: But this gift goes both ways. We’re both each other’s Party A and Party B.

284
00:24:21,343 --> 00:24:25,690
MC: My name is already written on it.

285
00:24:25,690 --> 00:24:28,855
MC: Lucien, are you willing?

286
00:24:28,855 --> 00:24:33,042
As I speak, Lucien takes another look at the ‘insurance policy’ in his hands.

287
00:24:33,042 --> 00:24:37,996
He reads very slowly, which even makes me a little nervous—was the content I prepared not rigorous enough, or was my wording too jocular?

288
00:24:37,996 --> 00:24:42,695
Or perhaps, it’s still too informal as a gift.

289
00:24:42,695 --> 00:24:46,754
Lucien: I do.

290
00:24:46,754 --> 00:24:51,964
As if it is the sound of fate itself, I hear his answer.

291
00:24:51,964 --> 00:25:00,114
Lucien: How fortunate I am to receive such a special gift.

292
00:25:00,114 --> 00:25:05,132
After saying this, Lucien takes a fountain pen from his pocket and signs his own name at the signature space, stroke by stroke.

293
00:25:05,132 --> 00:25:11,781
Last wisp of sunset sinks beneath the horizon, and the train plunges into darkness. Yet our names—mine on the left, Lucien’s on the right—remain clearly visible.

294
00:25:11,781 --> 00:25:20,219
The imprint left by ink upon the paper is deeply etched and powerful, like a vow both sincere and solemnly cherished.

295
00:25:21,593 --> 00:25:25,173
The train arrives at the station, and Lucien holds my hand as we step off.

296
00:25:25,173 --> 00:25:30,064
Standing on the dark platform, we seem to have arrived at some kind of endpoint as well.

297
00:25:30,064 --> 00:25:35,529
In the distance, the mountains and wilderness stand solemn; the distant soil seems to harbor a plethora of words that ‘time’ hasn’t yet finished speaking.

298
00:25:35,529 --> 00:25:42,529
Lucien: At a time like this, I suddenly don’t know what to say.

299
00:25:42,529 --> 00:25:48,346
I can’t help but smile. From my bag, I fish out the birthday candle I didn’t get to use during the day. I light it with the lighter I’d prepared and bring it close to him.

300
00:25:48,346 --> 00:25:52,661
MC: Then go ahead and make a wish. Happy birthday, Lucien.

301
00:25:52,661 --> 00:25:57,136
MC: When making a wish, you don’t have to say it.

302
00:25:57,136 --> 00:26:01,835
I wink at him.

303
00:26:01,835 --> 00:26:08,259
MC: The candle at noon wasn’t formal enough, and… you were just going along with the children back then, but you didn’t actually make a wish, right?

304
00:26:08,259 --> 00:26:11,935
Firelight flickers in his eyes, yet I feel there has never been a moment when I see him more clearly than now.

305
00:26:11,935 --> 00:26:15,419
Lucien chuckles.

306
00:26:15,419 --> 00:26:24,081
Lucien: Uh-oh, looks like I can’t hide anything from you anymore.

307
00:26:24,081 --> 00:26:28,620
MC: Then let me remind Mr. Xu here—you’ve just signed your name. If you deliberately try to conceal anything after this, you’ll have to…

308
00:26:28,620 --> 00:26:43,067
Lucien: Request the commence of a ‘confession session’ while simultaneously initiating ‘mandatory hug coverage’, carry out any necessary ‘compensatory acts’ as the situation requires, and reach a ‘reconciliation agreement’ in a timely manner.

309
00:26:43,067 --> 00:26:46,359
Lucien: I remember it all.

310
00:26:46,359 --> 00:26:50,514
He says it earnestly, as though it’s only natural. It makes me smile sheepishly.

311
00:26:50,514 --> 00:26:54,957
MC: .…Hurry up and make a wish!

312
00:26:54,957 --> 00:27:00,039
Lucien raises his hands to enclose mine, and together we reverently cradle the small candle.

313
00:27:00,039 --> 00:27:05,473
He gazes quietly at the flickering candle flame until it burns more than halfway down.

314
00:27:05,473 --> 00:27:09,692
I feel as though I can hear the wish he is confiding.

315
00:27:10,171 --> 00:27:16,532
At last, he looks at me, his eyes clear and bright, filled with all the world’s tenderness and heart-stirring affection.

316
00:27:16,532 --> 00:27:21,103
Lucien: I’ve made my wish.

317
00:27:21,103 --> 00:27:26,057
MC: Mhm! They will all come true.

318
00:27:27,176 --> 00:27:32,769
Lucien blows out the candle, and in the darkness, he kisses me.

319
00:27:32,769 --> 00:27:42,262
Lucien: I wish to share this brief yet brilliant life with you.

320
00:27:46,130 --> 00:27:49,102
[Personal musing]
He opens his eyes when makes his birthday wish, a small habit we’ve known since the first time we celebrated his birthday. Him closing his eyes while making a wish with the kids hints that he wasn’t truly wishing back then… xm writers and their attention to detail ;-;

321
00:27:49,901 --> 00:27:54,919
Why insurance as gift? Insurance is chosen because in general it exists to guard against risk and uncertainty, and that fear of uncertainty is precisely what he wrestles with throughout this date. He has always seen the world as transient and uncontrollable, but loving her and being with her for so long reintroduces fear that this uncertainty

322
00:27:54,919 --> 00:28:03,134
 might once again leave him alone. By giving him her ‘life insurance policy’, she is giving him a protection, a kind of promise that says ‘I commit my whole life to you. I choose to share this journey with you. No matter how uncertain the world is, you will not face it alone again’. 

323
00:28:03,134 --> 00:28:09,974
And I also love how both are each others’ party A and party B; insurer and the insured, meaning the commitment is mutual. Each of them is not only the one being protected, but also the one who assumes responsibility for protection,

324
00:28:09,974 --> 00:28:18,124
pledging their entire life to the other in equal measure. You can say that this mutual life-insurance pact becomes their own intimate, personal, and poetic version of a marriage certificate QwQ

325
00:28:20,202 --> 00:28:22,312
[Phone call- Lively Moment]

326
00:28:22,312 --> 00:28:29,439
Lucien: Sorry, looks like I’m running a bit later than the time we agreed upon.

327
00:28:29,439 --> 00:28:37,814
Lucien: The cake Pete and the others ordered was larger than I’d imagined. We talked for a while, and a lot of time had passed before I even realized it.

328
00:28:37,814 --> 00:28:42,800
Lucien: I’ve just gotten on the car. I hope your preparations won’t be delayed too much.

329
00:28:42,800 --> 00:28:47,690
MC: It’s okay, no need to rush.

330
00:28:47,690 --> 00:28:51,302
MC: Everyone at the Bioscience Research Center wanted to get together to celebrate your birthday and liven things up a bit. Staying a little longer wouldn’t really matter.

331
00:28:51,302 --> 00:28:57,119
Lucien: I didn’t expect everyone would actually go out of their way to put together a birthday party for me.

332
00:28:57,119 --> 00:29:00,539
Lucien: The institute never really had a tradition like this in previous years.

333
00:29:00,539 --> 00:29:03,384
MC: Just because there wasn’t one in previous years doesn’t mean there can’t be one from now on~ Maybe everyone’s been wanting to give you lots of good wishes for a long time already.

334
00:29:03,384 --> 00:29:06,133
MC: By the way, I seem to have heard from Pete that the students at Loveland University have apparently prepared some gifts for you as well.

335
00:29:06,133 --> 00:29:14,283
Lucien: Mm. Some former interns asked Pete to pass along their gifts, and a few PhD students prepared some things too.

336
00:29:14,283 --> 00:29:20,101
Lucien: But after accepting the kind sentiment, I entrusted Pete to return each of the gifts to them on my behalf.

337
00:29:20,101 --> 00:29:24,447
Lucien: As a teacher, it’s better to maintain proper distance from students.

338
00:29:24,447 --> 00:29:26,110
MC: You really did think everything through, Professor Xu.

339
00:29:26,110 --> 00:29:27,644
MC: But… this is really good~

340
00:29:27,644 --> 00:29:31,415
Lucien: Is it?

341
00:29:31,415 --> 00:29:34,452
MC: Yeah. Maybe I’m just being very cliché, but I hope every blessing finds its way to you, that everyone sends their good wishes your way.

342
00:29:34,452 --> 00:29:37,488
MC: It might be a bit too lively, but no matter what happens… I want to join the world in welcoming the day of your arrival.

343
00:29:37,488 --> 00:29:39,438
MC: I hope every warm moment can belong to you.

344
00:29:39,438 --> 00:29:41,164
MC: Would this kind of feeling make you feel troubled?

345
00:29:41,164 --> 00:29:44,169
Lucien: Fool, how could that be.

346
00:29:44,169 --> 00:29:49,826
Lucien: I’ve spent this day in many different ways, and with many different feelings.

347
00:29:49,826 --> 00:29:58,104
Lucien: But after having you by my side, it gradually came to hold more… unfamiliar, yet very warm moments.

348
00:29:58,104 --> 00:30:04,753
Lucien: And so, I’m able to walk back to some distant place, and touch many real feelings.

349
00:30:04,753 --> 00:30:08,556
Lucien: What you said is right. This is good.

350
00:30:08,556 --> 00:30:10,826
MC: Lucien, come home soon. I really wish I could hug you right now.

351
00:30:10,826 --> 00:30:16,451
Lucien: I think… this is probably my greatest wish at this moment too.

352
00:30:21,341 --> 00:30:24,314
The wind gently brushes across the lawn, carrying with it sunshine and the fragrance of flowers. In the courtyard, only the two of us remain.

353
00:30:24,314 --> 00:30:27,191
The whole world is held in the embrace of the afternoon light, bright and tranquil.

354
00:30:27,191 --> 00:30:31,378
The whole world is held in the embrace of the afternoon light, bright and tranquil.

355
00:30:31,378 --> 00:30:34,542
MC: Lucien, what are you thinking about right now?

356
00:30:35,022 --> 00:30:39,305
He blinks, his eyelashes brushing lightly against my palm.

357
00:30:39,305 --> 00:30:47,072
Lucien: I’m thinking… whether I might finally get to see that gift I’ve been looking forward to for so long.

358
00:30:47,072 --> 00:30:48,830
MC: ….?

359
00:30:48,830 --> 00:30:51,387
Perhaps sensing my momentary daze, he chuckles softly.

360
00:30:51,387 --> 00:30:55,574
Then, he holds back my hand and gently pulls me into his embrace.

361
00:30:55,574 --> 00:31:03,564
Lucien: Sorry, MC. Actually, I was wondering whether I should pretend I didn’t know anything just now.

362
00:31:03,564 --> 00:31:10,277
Lucien: But perhaps I was looking forward to it too much. I couldn’t hold back.

363
00:31:10,277 --> 00:31:13,825
Seeing the edges of his eyes turn up in self-satisfaction, with zero trace of apology, I can’t help but laugh.

364
00:31:13,825 --> 00:31:17,117
MC: Pfft, a certain birthday boy is clearly a year older now, so how come he’s becoming more and more like a little kid?

365
00:31:17,117 --> 00:31:23,637
Lucien: I can be even more like a little kid.

366
00:31:23,637 --> 00:31:28,112
Smiling, he looks at the handmade book in my hands and unabashedly holds out his palm.

367
00:31:28,112 --> 00:31:43,997
Lucien: If I could receive your gift right now, I think I’d be very happy.

368
00:31:45,148 --> 00:31:48,121
[Blow out the candle]

369
00:32:00,107 --> 00:32:07,906
“The candle flame lasts only a moment, but the bright eyes of a certain little lady will remain etched in my memory forever.”

370
00:32:27,020 --> 00:32:29,992
[Sing the birthday song]

371
00:33:18,096 --> 00:33:24,777
Lucien: Thank you for always bringing all the tenderness in the world before me.

372
00:33:27,493 --> 00:33:28,900
[Gift the pop-up book]

373
00:33:32,575 --> 00:33:39,160
Lucien: Such a cute little rabbit and little fox look like something MC made with her own hands.

374
00:33:39,160 --> 00:33:43,507
MC: The birthday boy has a keen eye~ So, any thoughts?

375
00:33:43,507 --> 00:33:49,803
Lucien: Although I haven’t opened it yet, I seem to be feeling so happy already.

376
00:33:49,803 --> 00:33:56,388
Lucien: The little fox’s warm scarf looks like something the little rabbit picked out with care.

377
00:33:56,388 --> 00:34:07,031
Lucien: Moreover, the little rabbit’s soft cheeks press close against him. Looks like it’s going to spend another incredibly warm winter.

378
00:34:07,031 --> 00:34:08,470
MC: Not just winter~

379
00:34:08,470 --> 00:34:12,753
MC: Whether it is the little fox in the fairy tale, or my little fox, they will both live a warm life.

380
00:34:12,753 --> 00:34:18,506
Lucien: Mm, I believe that too.

381
00:34:18,506 --> 00:34:25,218
Lucien: After all, the little rabbit will always stay by the little fox’s side.

382
00:34:27,839 --> 00:34:32,602
MC: Hehe, the first page is a birthday wish for Professor Lucien~

383
00:34:32,602 --> 00:34:43,054
Lucien: Little butterfly, dream catcher, Chinese bellflowers. It feels like being in a beautiful dream.

384
00:34:43,054 --> 00:34:46,697
MC: That’s right~ I hope you’ll have even more beautiful dreams in the coming year.

385
00:34:46,697 --> 00:34:50,469
MC: And as for me, I will be by your side every time you wake from a dream.

386
00:34:50,469 --> 00:34:58,588
Lucien: With a wish and promise like that from MC, it seems I have no choice but to obediently go to sleep.

387
00:34:58,588 --> 00:35:02,455
MC: That suits me just perfectly~ Look, there is another mechanism here.

388
00:35:02,455 --> 00:35:07,569
Lucien: It turns out this little butterfly is actually a candle.

389
00:35:07,569 --> 00:35:11,597
MC: Mm~ And it can be lit at any time. It will bless all your wishes and make them come true.

390
00:35:11,597 --> 00:35:20,067
Lucien: Rather than trouble it with my wishes, I think I’d rather watch it flutter freely through this secret garden.

391
00:35:20,067 --> 00:35:27,418
Lucien: After all, I’m much closer to another little butterfly.

392
00:35:28,473 --> 00:35:31,445
Lucien: Is this Loveland University’s lecture hall?

393
00:35:33,875 --> 00:35:37,263
MC: I knew you’d recognize it.

394
00:35:37,263 --> 00:35:41,386
MC: I wanted to recreate a glimpse of Professor Xu’s everyday life on this page.

395
00:35:41,386 --> 00:35:44,582
MC: Standing at the lectern, teaching and nurturing your students, imparting knowledge and wisdom… You always shine so brilliantly.

396
00:35:44,582 --> 00:35:51,774
Lucien: In that case, I’d like to invite little classmate MC to attend one of my classes next weekend.

397
00:35:51,774 --> 00:35:54,395
MC: Hmm? Don’t you usually have weekends off?

398
00:35:54,395 --> 00:36:00,883
Lucien: Originally, yes, but I’ve just made some changes to my schedule.

399
00:36:01,682 --> 00:36:07,979
Lucien: There will only be two of us in class that day.

400
00:36:07,979 --> 00:36:13,828
Lucien: As for the class content, how about we watch a romantic movie together?

401
00:36:13,828 --> 00:36:21,691
Lucien: And when the movie ends, that line on the whiteboard…. would you be willing to say it to me yourself?

402
00:36:26,102 --> 00:36:33,901
Lucien: In a parallel world, the little rabbit and the little fox are also in a beautiful garden.

403
00:36:33,901 --> 00:36:42,307
Lucien: But it seems I won’t have the chance today to paint a picture for my beloved little rabbit as the fox does.

404
00:36:42,307 --> 00:36:46,239
MC: But my mood seems even more jubilant than this little rabbit’s~

405
00:36:46,239 --> 00:36:49,147
Lucien: I feel the same way.

406
00:36:49,147 --> 00:36:59,887
Lucien: Perhaps saying this sounds a little boastful, but in every minute and every second of today, or perhaps not just today.

407
00:36:59,887 --> 00:37:07,366
Lucien: It seems that whenever MC thinks of me, or whenever her gaze falls upon me——

408
00:37:07,366 --> 00:37:16,060
Lucien: I feel that there is no one in this world happier or more fulfilled than I am.

409
00:37:18,777 --> 00:37:24,530
Lucien: These bubbles look very lifelike.

410
00:37:24,530 --> 00:37:28,206
MC: Hehe, I’ve been wanting to show off this part to you for ages~

411
00:37:28,206 --> 00:37:32,617
MC: Making these bubbles took the most time out of the entire handmade book. But looking at how it turned out, it was well worth it~

412
00:37:32,617 --> 00:37:38,977
Lucien: Mm, they’re beautiful and very dreamlike.

413
00:37:38,977 --> 00:37:46,361
Lucien: And they seem to hold some of MC’s lovely wishes too.

414
00:37:46,361 --> 00:37:50,196
MC: As expected, nothing gets past Professor Xu.

415
00:37:50,196 --> 00:37:54,607
MC: These bubbles will never disappear, nor they will ever burst.

416
00:37:54,607 --> 00:37:58,890
MC: As long as you wish, you can always grasp these beautiful fleeting moments.

417
00:37:58,890 --> 00:38:05,986
Lucien: I suddenly feel that their existence is just like MC.

418
00:38:05,986 --> 00:38:16,150
Lucien: Make me feel that my life truly can hold on to these miraculous fleeting moments forever.

419
00:38:19,315 --> 00:38:19,762
[Birthday celebration ends]

420
00:38:19,762 --> 00:38:24,397
Lucien closes the handmade book, yet his fingertips still linger cherishingly on its corner.

421
00:38:24,397 --> 00:38:29,990
Lucien: MC, I really love this gift. Thank you.

422
00:38:29,990 --> 00:38:34,369
MC: The birthday boy seems to have said “thank you” quite a few times today already~

423
00:38:34,369 --> 00:38:43,606
Lucien: Perhaps when a person is too happy, they really do become a bit clumsy.

424
00:38:43,606 --> 00:38:52,364
Lucien: There are so many things I want to say, but my brain… doesn’t quite seem to be keeping up.

425
00:38:52,364 --> 00:38:57,414
He shows a somewhat helpless expression, yet the corners of his lips unconsciously curl up into a faint smile.

426
00:38:57,414 --> 00:39:01,442
Finding him adorable, I can’t help but tilt my head and give him a kiss.

427
00:39:01,442 --> 00:39:06,140
MC: Then don’t say it. I know it all anyway.

428
00:39:06,140 --> 00:39:10,871
MC: Just like I know Professor Xu will be happy forever.

429
00:39:10,871 --> 00:39:14,387
The next second, he gently bends down and draws close to me.

430
00:39:14,387 --> 00:39:18,542
Before that kiss lands, I hear him whispers a wish, like murmurs spoken in a dream.

431
00:39:18,542 --> 00:39:31,199
Lucien: May you forever choose to anchor in my heart, hear all the words I cannot speak and all that I gladly bear.

432
00:39:31,391 --> 00:39:46,286
.
